      "permalink": "which-of-the-following-are-lewis-acids-2018-marks-4-vehsvlplszmhk22w.htm",
      "content": "Which of the following are Lewis acids?\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "BCl<sub>3</sub> and AlCl<sub>3</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "PH<sub>3</sub> and BCl<sub>3</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "AlCl<sub>3</sub> and SiCl<sub>4</sub> "
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "PH<sub>3</sub> and SiCl<sub>4</sub>\n"
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "A"
      ],
      "explanation": "The compound which have the ability to accepted at least are lone pair electron. \n<br><br>Structure of BCl<sub>3</sub> is \n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/raE4osQRcZPoKC6ue/2NFO7gy1SBew1Y78sw0E9ifpp4sGo/IhGOLt85jWISBdG0qiDtM7/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Ionic Equilibrium Question 119 English Explanation 1\">\n<br><br>Here B is electron deficient atom, so it can accepted lone pair. So it is a lewis acid. \n<br><br>Structure of AlCl<sub>3</sub> \n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/I9GrSw7cKV5v2Blsy/CjzAAPzcR9DpublfaNPQNmFgoRBGS/2AfMNxCkxn4YBCVg7y4g4n/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Ionic Equilibrium Question 119 English Explanation 2\">\n<br><br>Here, Al also a electron deficient atom so it has vacant orbital and in that vacant orbital it can take lone pair.  So it is also lewis acid. \n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/YftFTc2h6RyLQZLnL/8Nlp92YBlcF2sXNwWHZmRPGMh6MF2/JyYwR6k8p8G39rx4YDMPAs/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Ionic Equilibrium Question 119 English Explanation 3\">\n<br><br>Here in PH<sub>3</sub> there is vacant 3d orbital but it Can't take. Lone pair in 3d orbital because  P is more electro-negative than H so around P atom negative charge density is created and tendency of accepting electron decreases. So PH<sub>3</sub> is not lewis acid. \n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/xWiWefADHErMsSDVL/4429oloEd46Qrny72qvZBFEKd1Aya/dy3EZaBfMG9huQWqQ8L7bu/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Ionic Equilibrium Question 119 English Explanation 4\">\n<br><br>Here octet of Si full ut in has a tendency of accepting lone pair in vacant 3d orbital. \n<br><br>This can be shown by following reaction. \n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/VlZjBKIEqDrjmz9vf/oJ8gxtvIbXpVWASUzlUcZTRRqCUjB/oqkJJCNQjshTMaOYNKHAzM/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Ionic Equilibrium Question 119 English Explanation 5\">\n<br><br>So, here option (A) and (C) both are correct. But as SiCl<sub>4</sub> is not as strong lewis acid as BCl<sub>3</sub> and AlCl<sub>3</sub>, So  we can say option (A) is more correct."
    }
